# Greia images are built away from their eventual hardware, so boot-critical
# target drivers must never depend on build-host probing. Keep MODULES=most in
# conf.d/greia-hardware and let the greia-storage-modules hook conditionally add
# the broad x86 SATA/AHCI floor only when the TARGET kernel actually provides
# those modules. Future architecture profiles must extend that target-kernel /
# compatibility policy rather than hardcoding foreign modules in this shared file.
